Register the skills tool in cmd/launcher/main.go alongside the existing tools, following the mcp.Tool shape in internal/mcp/mcp.go.

Spec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-21-skill-subsystem-design.md sections 3.1 and 6.2.
Agent: unreagent-worker.

Acceptance:
- Description generated via DescribeAll so every skill name + one-line description is resident in the agent's context -- this is what makes one load call sufficient and is the reason MCP can be the default path
- parameters: name (required), section (optional sub-document)
- result: the skill body as text
- unknown name returns an error result that NAMES the available skills
- no list action -- the description already carries the list
- registered only when skills.enabled && skills.mcp
- defensive argument reading via the existing getString/firstString/errResult helpers

Depends on #9 and #10.
